commit f75ab3badf5d50a1eb4432b8bc4a8cbbdf343c9c
Author: Liz <liz@gewelf.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 21:51:08 2026 -0400

    perf(write): PLAIN page built in one buffer

    writeDataPageOptionalWithEncoding (fixed-width i32/i64/f32/f64/bool, PLAIN)
    and writeDataPageByteArrayOptionalWithEncoding (PLAIN) now build the page in a
    single buffer: def levels are appended in place, values are written straight
    into the buffer, and no intermediate non-null array or bool mask is allocated.
    Other encodings keep the general path.

    Bench (make bench, zig-only, 1M rows, best of 2 interleaved runs, HEAD vs this):
      int64_plain    write 26.13 -> 18.39 ms  (+42% rows/s; target +50%)
      f64_plain      write 26.82 -> 18.14 ms  (+48% rows/s; target +50%)
      int64_nullable write 19.94 -> 13.65 ms  (+46% rows/s; target +60%)
      str_unique     write 89.78 -> 80.21 ms  (+12% rows/s; target +10%)
      str_dict       write 57.94 -> 59.06 ms  (-2%, noise)
      mixed5         write 235.43 -> 214.55 ms (+10%)
      read paths unchanged
      file_MB unchanged: int64_plain 8000184 B, f64_plain 8000184 B,
      int64_nullable 5458529 B, str_dict 876940 B, str_unique 13889084 B, mixed5 21392746 B

    Tests: byte-identity against the general path (writeDataPageTypedWithEncoding
    for i64/f32/bool; encodeByteArraysWithEncoding + combineDefLevelsAndValues for
    byte arrays) over sizes, null rates and is_optional; NullInRequiredColumn and
    ValueTooLarge error order.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M67TEKZVVE2SZYMC9XJ6HNC0

